#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dece6a5a-e9b2-5531-85f0-3774d0e3f966" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Parametrization of a Hyperboloid of Two Sheets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b39f4a9-f6d2-56b9-924e-8172c150b7ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384747} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb6f395-3a76-55cb-945a-4de53a45c930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384748} {:answer/id #uuid "ac41a8d6-6c9d-57de-864a-8971e5fda4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384749} {:answer/id #uuid "97c2a13d-cdfd-57bb-81c0-d80d5af6dfbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384750} {:answer/id #uuid "b4cf0be2-d20b-5fc5-87d7-f8de8cf47691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97c2a13d-cdfd-57bb-81c0-d80d5af6dfbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384750} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b63eb85-2bf4-547a-a264-831e7ca376bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186384746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "500cb2cd-2289-5d53-9343-5bb7400db3ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-164576" :question/problem "The vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ),$ given by \n\n$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nparametrizes one sheet of the hyperboloid of two sheets defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-16.$ By expressing the equation of the hyperboloid in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the third component of $f.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the hyperbola ${z}^{2}-{r}^{2}={k}^{2}$ can be parametrized as $⟨z,r⟩=⟨k\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,k\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ⟩$* for $ϕ\\in R.$" :question/worked-solution "If $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical coordinates of a point and $(x,y,z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-16 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-16 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-{z}^{2} & =-16 \\\\ {r}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-16 \\\\ {z}^{2}-{r}^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the hyperbola ${z}^{2}-{r}^{2}=16$ represents the intersection of our hyperboloid with the plane that passes through the $z$-axis and makes the angle of $\\theta $ with the positive $x$-axis. Using the hint, a parametrization of such hyperbola can be given as\n\n$$\n⟨z,r⟩=⟨4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ⟩,\\,ϕ\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,(4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ.$"}]}
